WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.788
Let’s walk through Control arrival noise.

00:00:02.788 --> 00:00:06.362
Muting changes presentation noise, not workflow state.

00:00:06.362 --> 00:00:09.325
Use badges and NEW labels to locate unread work,

00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:12.363
then open the destination item so the durable arrival state

00:00:12.363 --> 00:00:14.338
clears for the correct reason.

00:00:14.338 --> 00:00:18.337
On this slide, mute notifications suppresses durable arrival notices

00:00:18.337 --> 00:00:19.325
only.

00:00:19.325 --> 00:00:23.050
Badges and NEW labels remain visible until each destination item

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.188
is opened.

00:00:24.188 --> 00:00:28.225
In practice, mute presentation noise without hiding unread work

00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:29.887
or changing queue state.

00:00:30.385 --> 00:00:33.835
When you are ready, use Focus notification control to

00:00:33.835 --> 00:00:35.698
move to the live surface.

00:00:35.698 --> 00:00:38.485
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:38.485 --> 00:00:38.635
.
